Add IORPC.kernelContent for Xcode 16's iig.

xnu-8796 (macOS 13.5) predates this field. Xcode 15.x's iig did not emit
references to it, which is why the build pinned runs-on: macos-14 -- the
last GitHub-hosted image carrying Xcode 15.x. That image is retired
("The configuration 'macos-14-arm64-us-default' is not supported"), and
macos-15 ships Xcode 16.0 through 26.3 with no 15.x at all, so the pin
cannot be restored. Installing Xcode 15.4 via xcodes needs Apple
Developer credentials.

Current xnu adds the member kernel-only; this is that change, applied to
both copies of the header exactly as upstream has it:

    https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h

The field is declared but never populated here. Nothing in this port runs
a DriverKit user server, so the RPC path that would read it is not
exercised; if a dext is ever loaded, IOUserServer would need the matching
change too.

--- a/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
+++ b/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
@@ -224,6 +224,9 @@
 	IORPCMessageMach * reply;
 	uint32_t           sendSize;
 	uint32_t           replySize;
+#ifdef KERNEL
+	IORPCMessage     * kernelContent;
+#endif /* KERNEL */
 };
 typedef struct IORPC IORPC;
 
--- a/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
+++ b/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
@@ -224,6 +224,9 @@
 	IORPCMessageMach * reply;
 	uint32_t           sendSize;
 	uint32_t           replySize;
+#ifdef KERNEL
+	IORPCMessage     * kernelContent;
+#endif /* KERNEL */
 };
 typedef struct IORPC IORPC;
 
